# a waker ends the poll of another thread; a pipe written with writeq
# gives -32 when nobody reads, and the signal stays away
buf ev 32
buf fds 8
buf st 16
fn other w
	rt sleep 30000000
	rt wakeup w
end
rt poller as ep
rt waker as w
rt watch ep w 1 7 as a
rt poll ep ev 2 0 as none
ref other as f
rt thread f w
rt poll ep ev 2 5000 as n
load ev as what
load ev+8 as tag
sys pipe fds
load4 fds as r
load4 fds+4 as wr
rt writeq wr "ab" as ok
rt close r
rt writeq wr "ab" as gone
rt exit (a==0)+(none==0)*2+(n==1)*4+(what==1)*8+(tag==7)*16+(ok==2)*32+(gone==-32)*64
